 <h2 align="center"><strong>Fifth National Conference on Space Science & Technology (NCSS&T-2017) </strong> </h2>
  <p>The  Institute of Space Science and Technology, University of Karachi is  organizing the Fifth National Conference on Space Science &amp; Technology on  October 9-10, 2017 at University of Karachi for celebrating &quot;World Space  Week 2017&quot;. This conference is being organized in collaboration with  SUPARCO and Higher Education Commission. The main theme of the Conference is &ldquo;<strong>Exploring New Worlds in Space</strong>&rdquo;.  The Vice Chancellor, Prof. Dr. Muhammad Ajmal Khan will preside while Dean,  Faculty of Science, Prof. Dr. Tasneem Adam Ali will also be present at this  occasion.</p>
  <p><strong>The invited speakers are Prof.  Dr. Asghar Qadir (</strong>Hilal-e-Imtiaz &amp; Sitara-e-Imtiaz<strong>)&nbsp;from NUST, Islamabad; Dr. Hafeez Hoorani from National Center for  Physics, Islamabad; Prof. Dr. Hamid Saleem from Institute of Space Technology,  Islamabad;&nbsp;Prof. Dr. Muhammad Sharif (Tamgha-e-Imtiaz) from University of  Punjab, Lahore; Dr. Ihtzaz Qamar from KRL (former Member), Islamabad; </strong>Dr.  Zahida Ehsan from COMSATS Institute of Information Technology, Lahore; Dr.  Najam Abbas Naqvi from <strong>Institute of Space Technology,  Islamabad;&nbsp;Dr. Khan Alam from University of Peshawar;</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Dr. Nouman Qureshi from G. C. University, Lahore; Dr. Muhammad Shahid  from</strong>Women University Azad Jammu &amp; Kashmir, Bagh; Dr.  Gulzar Khan from Abdul Wali Khan University Mardan, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa<strong>; </strong><strong>Prof. Dr. M. Ayub Khan Yousufzai and Prof. Dr. Syed Jamil H. Kazmi from  University of Karachi.</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>Prof.  Dr. M. Jawed Iqbal is the Conference Convener, Dr. Mirza Jawwad Baig is the  Secretary, Mr. Fayyaz-ur-Rasheed is the Joint Secretary, Mr. Faisal Ahmed Khan  Afridi, Mr. Syed Faisal-ur-Rehman and Ms. Hira Fatima are the Assistant  Secretary while 14 other members are included in the Conference Organizing  Committee.</p>
